IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ca-ownership`

-- Copyright Act 1968 (Cth) -- worked cases from the seat of the employee-author and the founder.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case (on originality, on "contract of service", on "in pursuance of the terms of" employment, or on computer
-- programs), against the regulations under s 184, or against practice.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_copyright-act-1968_baseline.py). Expected
-- results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- The life event: Daniel, d046 (1 September 2031) -- "the code owned by the company". Facts the scenario does not state are
-- ASSUMPTIONS, labelled where used: that Jarrah's engineers are employees under contracts of service who wrote the matching
-- engine as part of their jobs; that the engine was written in Perth by Australian residents and has not been published;
-- that Daniel, as founder-director, had no employment contract of his own; and the engineer's year of death (2070),
-- which is ILLUSTRATIVE.

