§ `s 35 -- who first owns it`

-- d046: the engine written by Jarrah's employed engineers belongs to Jarrah by s 35(6).
#ASSERT `Who first owns the copyright in what I made` `Jarrah's matching engine` `an engineer employed by Jarrah, writing it as part of the job` EQUALS `the author's employer`
#ASSERT `Who first owns the copyright in what I made` `Jarrah's matching engine` `an employee writing a weekend side project outside her duties` EQUALS `the author`
#ASSERT `Who first owns the copyright in what I made` `Jarrah's matching engine` `a contractor paid to write it` EQUALS `the author`
#ASSERT `Who first owns the copyright in what I made` `Jarrah's matching engine` `Daniel, founder-director with no employment contract` EQUALS `the author`
#ASSERT `Who first owns the copyright in what I made` `Jarrah's matching engine` `an employee whose contract lets her keep the copyright` EQUALS `the author`
#ASSERT `Who first owns the copyright in what I made` `a feature article` `a staff journalist writing for the paper` EQUALS `the periodical proprietor, except the author's book and facsimile rights`
#ASSERT `Who first owns the copyright in what I made` `a wedding photograph` `a photographer paid by the couple` EQUALS `the person who commissioned it`
#ASSERT `Who first owns the copyright in what I made` `code copied from someone else's repository` `an engineer employed by Jarrah, writing it as part of the job` EQUALS `nobody, because no copyright subsists`

